<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chiaramonte family</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th–14th centuries</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Chiaramonte</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Chiaramonte were a Sicilian baronial family, counts of Modica, who became one of the most powerful houses of the island under the Aragonese kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> in the fourteenth century. They built the Palazzo Chiaramonte, known as the Steri, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palermo">Palermo</a>. Their power ended when Andrea Chiaramonte resisted the Aragonese restoration and was executed in Palermo in 1392.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chiaramonte-family.jpg" alt="Chiaramonte family" width="320" height="352" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jmirache · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blas%C3%B3n_de_la_Casa_de_Chiaromonte.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
